    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537229/parttime-lecturer-in-population-and-policy-analysis": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Part-Time Lecturer in Population and Policy Analysis The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537229 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for the appointment as Part-time Lecturer in Population and Policy Analysis in the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref. 537229) , to commence in December 2026 or as soon as possible on temporary term, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a Master’s degree in Public Policy, Public Administration, or a related field.  They should demonstrate a strong record of either professional practice in policy design and evaluation within institutional settings (e.g., government, NGOs, or consultancy firms), and/or prior teaching experience of similar applied policy courses.  Familiarity with drafting policy proposals, agenda-setting, consultations, conducting stakeholder analyses, and applying practical evaluation frameworks (such as logic models or cost-benefit reasoning) is highly desirable.  Knowledge of the policy environment in Greater China or East Asia is an advantage.  A background in demography, population studies, or quantitative/statistical modelling is not a must. The appointee will teach the course \"Applied Policy Design and Strategy,\" a generalist elective course offered by the Master of Social Sciences in the field of Population and Policy Analysis programme.  He/She will be responsible for developing course materials, and delivering lectures and tutorials throughout a standard 12-week semester.  The appointee will be supported by a Teaching Assistant, who will assist with course-related administrative duties and grading tasks. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload (1) an up-to-date C.V.; (2) a cover letter; (3) a one-page teaching statement, (4) the contact information of three senior referees familiar with the applicant's academic and professional background; and (5) a teaching portfolio (less than 50MB).  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until September 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537229 Part-Time Lecturer in Population and Policy Analysis Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Sep 30, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537229 Part-Time Lecturer in Population and Policy Analysis Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Sep 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537230/student-advising-officer-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537230 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Student Engagement and Leadership of Centre of Development and Resources for Students (Ref.: 537230) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary/ Renewal of contract is subject to the availability of project funding and mutual agreement.). Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree with at least 3-5 years' relevant post-qualification experience, preferably with some experience in database and online platform management. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); strong communication, organizational and problem-solving skills, and the ability to work independently with initiative and under pressure to meet tight deadlines. They should also be a good team player with the ability to multitask, be attentive to details, and have a strong sense of responsibility. The appointee will Oversee the administration and daily operation of two Amenities Centres, including financial administration, budget control, maintenance and improvement works, contractor and support staff supervision, venue utilisation, safety and security; Liaising with student societies, student leaders, hall/college representatives, University units, and external partners on matters relating to student activities, leadership development, and student support; Planning, coordinating, implementing and evaluating student leadership development, orientation, integration, cultural exchange, and campus-wide engagement programmes that promote students' holistic development and enrich campus life. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until September 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 1, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537230 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Oct 1, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537230 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Oct 1, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537231/clerk-i-holding-the-functional-title-of-senior-executive-assistant-in-the-department-of-geography-ref537231": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) in the Department of Geography (Ref.:537231) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537231 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Geography (30900) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong We are looking for a Senior Executive Assistant to join the Department of Geography. The Role The appointee will play a pivotal role in the General Office, reporting to the Head of the Department, the Deputy Head of Department for Teaching and Learning, and the Director of Undergraduate Studies. He/She will oversee the day-to-day operations of undergraduate programmes (including course timetabling, enrolment management, syllabus updates, and examinations); serve as the primary frontline point of contact for undergraduate student inquiries and advising; assist in coordinating curriculum review processes and external assessment exercises; manage the preparation and regular updating of programme-related materials; support outreach activities and alumni relations; assist in organizing departmental events; and perform other administrative duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities A Bachelor's degree in Geography or a related discipline; At least 1 year of relevant, full-time administrative work experience (experience in tertiary education administration or undergraduate programme support is highly preferred); A good command of spoken and written English and Chinese (including Cantonese and Putonghua); Excellent communication, organizational and problem-solving skills, with meticulous attention to detail; IT proficiency (including Microsoft Office; familiarity with university administration systems such as Moodle is an advantage), with the ability to multitask; A good team player, self-motivated, capable of working independently and collaborating effectively with different academic units, staff, and students; A strong sense of responsibility and an unwavering commitment to ethical conduct, transparency, and collegiality. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV and a tailored cover letter. Review of applications will start on September 15, 2026 , and continue until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Advertised: Sep 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537231 Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) in the Department of Geography (Ref.:537231) Department of Geography (30900) Sep 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537231 Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) in the Department of Geography (Ref.:537231) Department of Geography (30900) Sep 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537242/executive-officer-clerk-ii-holding-the-functional-title-of-programme-manager-executive-assistant": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Executive Officer / Clerk II (holding the functional title of Programme Manager / Executive Assistant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537242 Work type: Full-time Department: Academic Liaison Office of the Registry (60380) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer / Clerk II (holding the functional title of Programme Manager / Executive Assistant) in the Academic Liaison Office of the Registry (several posts) (Ref: 537242) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, and with the possibility of renewal) The Academic Liaison Office, which includes International Affairs Office, Mainland Affairs Office and HKU Summer Institute, is dedicated to promoting academic exchanges and fostering collaboration with Mainland and overseas institutions.  We are looking for talented individuals to join our team as we grow. Applicants should have a good Bachelor's degree, preferably with at least 3 years' work experience in tertiary institutions.  They should also have a good command of spoken and written English and Chinese (fluency in Putonghua would be an advantage); good organisational, communication and problem-solving skills; as well as an outgoing personality.  They should possess the ability to work independently with initiative; lead projects; and be able to work under pressure. The appointees will be responsible for the development and management of programmes for the HKU Summer Institute, liaising with departments within the University, overseas institutions and external organisations, student recruitment, bookkeeping, general office administrative duties, and performing any other duties as assigned by the Office Head.  They may be required to work outside normal office hours and on weekends.  Occasional travel may be required.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Executive Assistant. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until September 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537249/project-officer-at-the-rank-of-clerk-ii": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537249 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk II) in the HKU Research Hub of Population Studies (the Population Hub), Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537249) ( https://www.socsc.hku.hk/rhps/ ), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or equivalent, with 1-3 years of proven experience, preferably in a tertiary institution.  They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); a strong sense of responsibility; excellent organisational, interpersonal, and communication skills; good IT proficiency; and be able to work independently in a team, attentive to details and handle multiple tasks with self-motivation and prioritise effectively under tight deadlines. This appointee will provide support to the Population Hub, including (a) assisting in events and knowledge exchange activities and visits, (b) providing support in answering enquiries, (c) maintaining webpages and managing records and bookings, (d) assisting in general office administration, and (e) performing other duties as assigned.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until September 18, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 18, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537249 Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk II) Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Sep 18, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537249 Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk II) Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Sep 18, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
