    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537183/executive-officer-holding-the-functional-title-of-assistant-manager-in-the-hong-kong-jockey-club-global-health-institute-hkjcghi": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Assistant Manager) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537183 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Assistant Manager) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health (Ref.: 537183), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. HKU has partnered with the International Vaccine Institute (IVI) and The University of Cambridge to establish the HKJCGHI, funded by the Hong Kong Jockey Club Charities Trust. IVI is a non-profit international organisation dedicated to vaccines and vaccination for global health. IVI coordinates the epidemiology, pandemic preparedness, vaccine process development, and capacity-building workstreams of the HKJCGHI. These areas of work are integrated with HKJCGHI activities through IVI Headquarters in Seoul. Applicants should possess a recognized Bachelor’s degree with at least 5 years of relevant work experience, preferably in tertiary institutions. They should have a strong command of written and spoken English and Chinese; good computer proficiency, especially in Microsoft Office applications; strong organisational and communication skills; and the ability to work independently as well as in a team. The successful candidate should be detail-oriented, self-motivated, able to prioritize multiple tasks efficiently, and capable of producing high-quality work under pressure and within tight deadlines. The appointee will join the IVI team, primarily supporting vaccine process development, with additional involvement in other IVI workstreams as required. He/She will provide ad hoc and non-routine administrative support for IVI-led workstreams. Responsibilities include supporting the organization of academic activities and events such as training workshops, seminars, and conferences; managing financial operations and coordinating human resources activities, including recruitment, onboarding, and visa applications; ensuring timely reporting, streamlining procedures, and maintaining stakeholder relationships; overseeing procurement, budgeting, and financial reporting; managing research project budgets and resources; collaborating with internal and external stakeholders to support project implementation and event management; addressing operational challenges and maintaining efficient office operations; coordinating with research and administrative teams; managing laboratory facilities; and performing other duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from September 15, 2026 and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 1, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537183 Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Assistant Manager) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) School of Public Health (22400) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537183 Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Assistant Manager) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) School of Public Health (22400) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537214/administrative-assistant-ii-executive-officer-in-the-department-of-social-work-and-social-administration": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Administrative Assistant II / Executive Officer in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537214 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Administrative Assistant II /Executive Officer in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (Ref.: 537214), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and a University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above, with at least 6 years of relevant administrative work experience in a tertiary education setting. They should have an excellent command of English and Chinese, good organisational, problem-solving, communication and interpersonal skills, and very good IT proficiency. The applicants should also demonstrate a strong sense of responsibility, be someone who can take the initiative, be independent, and prioritise multiple tasks efficiently to meet strict deadlines with minimal supervision. They should also be tactful in dealing with sensitive and confidential issues and have prior experience in handling HR, financial and general office administration independently, preferably for a research team of 30 people or more. Those with less experience or qualifications may be considered for the Executive Officer. The appointee will support the Principal Investigator and the Project Managers in overseeing project development, operations and management. S/he will build and maintain strong relationships with stakeholders, such as the co-investigators, the funder, academic and research staff members, social service providers, administrative, and IT technical professionals. They will also create and maintain comprehensive project documentation, plans and reports, manage the team’s financial and HR matters, deliver various administrative tasks for project dissemination, and perform other project administrative and secretarial duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until September 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 1, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537214 Administrative Assistant II / Executive Officer in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Sep 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537214 Administrative Assistant II / Executive Officer in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Sep 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
